E</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">COUCHE MINCE ET COMPOSANT A SEMI-CONDUCTEUR</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-2140925-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>2140925</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-62237767-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>62237767</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6283589-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6283589</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8227167-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8227167</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1134794A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIHARA TAKAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANEGAFUCHI CHEMICAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIHARA, TAKAFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI, MASASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIHARA TAKAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIHARA, TAKAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI, MASASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A semiconductor thin film contains, as main constituent elements, a group-IV element and hydrogen which are deposited under the condition that the temperature of the substrate is below 400  DEG C by chemical vapor deposition. The amount of hydrogen atoms released from the thin film when the thin film is heated from room temperature has a raised-temperature dependence shown by a curve of which the profile has a peak in a range from 370  DEG C to 410  DEG C. The half width of the peak is below 30  DEG C. There is also disclosed a thin film device having a semiconductor unit including such a semiconductor thin film and an electrode unit including a conductive thin film, both units formed on the same substrate.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Couche mince de semi-conducteur contenant, en tant que constituants principaux, un élément de groupe IV et de l'hydrogène déposés dans des conditions de température du substrat inférieure à 400  DEG C par un procédé de dépôt chimique en phase vapeur. La quantité d'atomes d'hydrogène libérés de la couche mince quand on réchauffe cette dernière depuis la température ambiante est dépendante de l'élévation de la température, comme le montre une courbe dont le profil présente une crête dans une plage située entre 370  DEG C et 410  DEG C. La moitié de la largeur de la crête est inférieure à 30  DEG C. L'invention concerne également un composant à couche mince possédant une partie semi-conducteur comprenant cette couche mince et une partie électrode comprenant une couche mince conductrice, ces deux parties étant constituées sur le même substrat.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>